# claude.agent - Claude Code, the default agent.
# `go` continues the most recent conversation, falling back to a fresh session
# when there is none: `claude --continue` errors "No conversation found" on a
# fresh project rather than starting fresh, so the `|| claude` is load-bearing.
# `resume` picks a conversation. Two keys, each a shell command; mux runs the
# one for the verb (go/resume) as the agent pane's process. --bare runs neither.
go      claude --continue || claude
resume  claude --resume

# busy: a string that appears in the pane ONLY while a turn is in progress.
# `mux agent-doctor` uses it to settle the one case CPU cannot: a record saying
# `working` while the agent actually sits at a prompt. Claude Code shows an
# interrupt affordance in its footer for exactly the duration of a turn.
#
# Validated against 12 live panes across two machines: present on every pane
# whose record said `working`, absent on every `idle` one, no exceptions.
#
# OPTIONAL. An agent with no `busy` line simply leaves the doctor where it was,
# reporting a quiet working agent as mid-turn rather than calling it stale.
busy    esc to interrupt
